{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/976994-dragon-blooded-in-malfeas","id":976994,"title":"Dragon-Blooded in Malfeas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T23:05:56-07:00","id":976994,"title":"Dragon-Blooded in Malfeas?","content":"I split this off from the Headcannon because it isn't really my headcannon, but a half-baked idea that I'd like feedback on.<br /> <br /> <br /> I prefer the Games of Divinity, &quot;Few Infernal Exalted [akuma] exist in this age.&quot; to the 2e Reclamation legions of akuma with Yozi Charms, Sidereal MA, and Solar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I also can't see the demons <b><i>not</i></b> trying at some point to use Terrestrial akuma to breed a gens in Hell itself, as loyal source of new akuma. So I wrote this:<br /> <br /> <br /> The Yozis don't have entire legions of Exalted akuma, but the Unquestionable have adapted to the considerable difficulties of actually persuading Exalted to serve them. During the late First Age, certain Third Circles directed their Terrestrial akuma to found Gens Metap\u0101i in Malfeas. The gens has slowly grown over the past two-plus millennia to almost half the size of the modern Seventh Legion. Their breeding is no better than the Scarlet Dynasty's, having inevitably became diluted with demon and mortal blood \u2013 usually they use neomah to reproduce anyway. Members are raised from birth to worship the Yozis, and Unquestionable approach them at Exaltation to bid for their service. Most accept... but there have been a handful who preferred to remain free agents of Hell, and a few who rebelled altogether. No dynasty Charm can force an Investiture. Metap\u0101i are a valuable resource, but keeping them loyal requires both limiting their exposure to Creation until after their Investiture, and granting them a better life than that of mortal and First Circle slaves until and unless they fail to exalt. Their demon-blooded nature, unfamiliarity with Creation, and lack of legitimate (non-cultic) Dragon-Blooded connections hamper their subtlety and effectiveness in Creation. (Their familiarity with Hell does make them very useful for intrigue and attacks against other demons' holdings.) They still outnumber Creation-born akuma because not many Exalted are willing to serve the Yozis, even not knowing the details of the Investiture.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I admit that I don't have <i><b>any</b></i> clear idea how successful such an attempt would actually be. My crude number-crunching may have badly underestimated the mortality rates these guys would have -- it was the least-informed number in my attempted population calculation. I'm not sure if I even like this idea for sure. I can imagine an alternative scenario in which they're all but wiped out by Unquestionable fighting over who will control the gens.<br /> <br /> I didn't write down the numbers I used, but I assumed a starting population of 5, negligible input of new blood from Creation, and reproducing very rarely. They can use a neomah whenever they want, but it takes time to raise and train a human child, and not all of the childrearing and Exalted training can be accomplished by demons. Nor should the slaves descended from those who failed to exalt (or who were purchased from the Guild) be allowed much influence over children who may yet exalt, nor pubescent teens who might <i>breed</i> with them. But akuma have jobs to do, and compulsions to obsess over their Urges, so they won't often take the time to raise a kid. I treated that as the biggest limitation on how fast their numbers would grow, and also assumed nearly half were in Creation during the Contagion and died.<br /> <br /> Feedback? If demons actually attempted to do this, what do you think the likely outcome would actually be? Would they succeed in breeding them and then not destroying them with fights over who controls them? Would concentrating the handpuppets of separate demons in one place lead to them killing each other? Would their breeding end up more diluted? Would their population be much larger than I projected? Would they be 100% loyal, or defecting left and right? Is it silly to think any Third Circles would even attempt this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-27-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:15:27-07:00","id":977031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/976994-dragon-blooded-in-malfeas#post976994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't write down the numbers I used, but I assumed a starting population of 5, negligible input of new blood from Creation, and reproducing very rarely. They can use a neomah whenever they want, but it takes time to raise and train a human child, and not all of the childrearing and Exalted training can be accomplished by demons. Nor should the slaves descended from those who failed to exalt (or who were purchased from the Guild) be allowed much influence over children who may yet exalt, nor pubescent teens who might <i>breed</i> with them. But akuma have jobs to do, and compulsions to obsess over their Urges, so they won't often take the time to raise a kid. I treated that as the biggest limitation on how fast their numbers would grow, and also assumed nearly half were in Creation during the Contagion and died.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, <b>CoCD:Malfeas</b> established that hell has a soul shortage; they must import mortal souls to make up for constant loss.<br /> <br /> The Yozis have no claim on the souls of any mortal who dies in Malfeas. unless they had voluntarily allowed the Yozis to place a lien on their soul in life; otherwise the souls of the slain return straight to Creation, the Underworld, or Oblivion. Further, the only way a mortal child can be borne live in Malfeas is if the Yozis take one of the hell trapped ghosts and bathe it in the Lethe to reincarnate the cleansed soul. Unfortunately for the Yozis, this frees that soul from their claim, so they must persuade the reborn to freely pledge its soul before it dies, and hell isn't a safe place to raise children even when its denizen try to take care of them.<br /> <br /> ( &quot;The baby was crying, so I swaddled it up snuggly in my limbs and let it suckle on my secretions. It was happy numbing on my juices, yes it was. They are nutritious and delicious. The baby liked them so much and wanted more, and more, and more. Then it grabbed my sweaty little body and shoved it in its mouth. It struggled for a little while, but now its nice and still. So I did good, okay? Only... now I'm stuck and its so cold and dark in here. Actually, it's kind of pleasant, but I have work to do. Can you get me out now?&quot; )<br /> <br /> Anyhow, the slaves who failed to exalt will be cultists, and raise the children to be the same, knowing that a select few will be chosen by the Yozii to be akuma, and the others, if they serve well in life and death, will be rewarded with a chance to reincarnate and exalt as akuma in their next lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-27-2016, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:34:32-07:00","id":977041,"title":"","content":"I didn't know about the soul shortage. That probably makes the whole concept impossible, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> But I was envisioning that the Akuma or human slaves would have to care for each baby near-constantly for the first few years because... well, none of the other canon demon options are much good, either. Although Leliel did invent <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/338408-new-demon-omsorgi-the-armored-nurses\">a species solely for this purpose</a>. It isn't the best option either, but it won't kill or eat or abandon that baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-27-2016, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:07:22-07:00","id":978880,"title":"","content":"I did something like this years ago in a campaign. But the Yozi's DB project was in a secluded area of Creation hidden from Yu Shan and the Loom by a Sidereal akuma. A secret city hidden in the mountains in the North. All people raised to be fanatically loyal to House Iselsi and their patron Yozi. After 400 years the project managed to generate about 1,000 DBs.<br /> <br /> So, I think it's doable but probably not in Malfeas. It'll probably have to be in Creation somewhere or an island of reality in the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:40:56-07:00","id":978962,"title":"","content":"That many Dragon-Blooded Akuma could probably make mincemeat of the Realm and Lookshy.<br /> <br /> The Investiture of Infernal Glory literally lets the Yozi play around with the dots on someone's character sheet and ignore normal limits, even before you get to Yozi charms they're capable of making anyone peerless in a given field and free of the quirks and distractions that invariably plague the best at what they do.<br /> Urge is only really a complication if the Yozi is treating this like a genuine pact between themselves and the Exalt like \u201cgive me the strength to destroy the Bull of the North and avenge the Tepet Legions and I will be yours in mind, body and soul\u201d raising Exalts that you expect to offer these things because they've been raised their entire life to know of no higher calling circumvents that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:25:06-07:00","id":979606,"title":"","content":"Expanding on my previous point and addressing this directly. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/976994-dragon-blooded-in-malfeas#post976994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I also can't see the demons <b><i>not</i></b> trying at some point to use Terrestrial akuma to breed a gens in Hell itself, as loyal source of new akuma.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the main reason the situation with Akuma has persisted as long as it has is because the Yozis limited the majority of their recruitment to sorcerers who wanted to make a pact. Trying to force the Investiture on captive exalts or building an army of Exalts loyal to Hell is the sort of thing that would invite reprisals to remind them who lost the Primordial War.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:13:03-07:00","id":979636,"title":"","content":"From a purely practical POV, you need ways for babies to survive M's environmental hazards. Air is toxic. If your orphanage is on the surface, it occasionally gets smashed by colliding layers. Build it underground, and you have the problem of stuff that live in the dark. Then there is the killer winds, non-musicality of crying babies, floods of vitriol, random demons thinking they can get away with eating the not-yet-exalted humans when no one is looking. What happens when Erembor or Hegra come by? Have fixes for all of that and you're in business. Maybe dress the babies all in forbidden blue to keep them safe from random demons?<br /> <br /> Easier to do it in Creation, say fostering with the Lintha. And in a lot of ways, isn't this basically what the Lintha are? (proto-exalts so they can have charms, demon-worshipping so easy to invest, etc etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","user":"SpoonR","date":".  Forgot the sound of silence 10-01-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:51:33-07:00","id":980363,"title":"","content":"&quot;Toxic air&quot; usually gets ignored since it only shut down stories and was a pretty stupid 2e-ism.<br /> <br /> On that note, maybe EarthScorpion's Men of Malfeas might be of interest: <a href=\"http://directforums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/in-the-mind-of-a-green-sun-prince-exalted-nasuverse.23111/page-22#post-4623561\" target=\"_blank\">http://directforums.sufficientveloci...2#post-4623561</a><br /> <br /> (Or rather, what we managed to preserve.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:26:25-07:00","id":983861,"title":"","content":"Don't know how exactly it would fit in your ideas or not, but once i played with the concept of a neomah-crafted child that managed to somehow survive in Malfeas long enough to reach adolescence and then exalt as a terrestrial - and when one stops to think that neomahs will take samples for basically every work they do, the idea of them spawning a bunch of kids with such potential just through serving some DB sorcerer for a long time is not all that far-fetched. The main challenge is in either if they still count as mortal after being given life by a neomah tower's flame, what can vary depending on a ST's preferences, and their continued survival up to puberty or adulthood in Malfeas, a very improbable prospect for any abandoned newborn that is not adopted/kept by some being willing to care for and protect it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, i have played with the idea of some particular demons or peculiar individuals living in Malfeas making up such &quot;neomah-spawn herds&quot; for a variety of reasons and interest, exotic, mundane or obscure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2016, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:28:38-07:00","id":984035,"title":"","content":"If a Neomah is told to craft a baby using only human parts, the result is a human child and usually not even demon-blooded.<br /> <br /> If they're just throwing together whatever they have for their personal projects, it depends entirely on who and what they've had sex with in the last [unknown span of time].<br /> <br /> <br /> Having read EarthScorpion's Men of Malfeas, I thought it made sense for there to be a population of humans living in Hell as slaves. His reason for why they can be born with 2 souls is that a soul needs 5 days to leave Hell and reach Lethe, and if a baby is born during those 5 days they have to reincarnate before reaching Lethe. This is a non-canon interpretation of course -- you could easily say that Lethe is a phenomenon, not a place, and transcends the separation between realms. Or that human souls cannot return to life until they pass through Lethe. But that was ES's reasoning.<br /> <br /> He also ignored the dumb &quot;poison miasma air&quot; thing and described in detail how humans can survive and raise children even when not kept alive for slave labor.<br /> <br /> Thinking more about breeding infernalist DBs in Hell (or in Creation), though, I realized that it's very unlikely for one Third Circle to have enough DB akuma of their own to start a sustainable bloodline, and also highly unlikely for multiple Third Circles to work together by lending multiple akuma to such a project. They'd have to agree on who would control the offspring and get dibs on them. So any such project would probably start with just one or two DBs. Then you need to use human cultists to raise them (or import cultists into Hell) because babysitting is a waste of an akuma's time. And unless you keep the brothers and sisters marrying each other every generation, the blood will get very thin very fast.<br /> <br /> (Then you need the cultists to react with more intelligence than that Salmalin imbecile who chased Harmonious Jade out of the cult.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if there are Men of Malfeas, the occasional individual might exalt as a DB, once in a great while. And if they're just 'street people' descended from slaves and not especially loyal to the Yozis, they're not necessarily going to want to be akuma. Not when being Exalted might mean a chance to escape into Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-08-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:10:33-07:00","id":984055,"title":"","content":"I once played a game with a new group where everyone else at the table was adamant that it was textually supported (or at least textually implied) that Malfeas had demonic breeding factories that had turned out <i>millions</i> of Dragon-Blooded akuma since the First Age as an invasion force.<br /> <br /> I left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:28:19-07:00","id":984180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/976994-dragon-blooded-in-malfeas?p=984035#post984035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Neomah is told to craft a baby using only human parts, the result is a human child and usually not even demon-blooded.<br /> <br /> If they're just throwing together whatever they have for their personal projects, it depends entirely on who and what they've had sex with in the last [unknown span of time].</div> </div> </div> </div>True in both instances, though a child made from only (or mostly) human parts might have some slim chance of exalting as such if at least some of the material used came from one or more dragon-blooded sorcerers it has served.<br /> <br /> It's not anything like a science, specially when it comes to such an unplanned bonus in the crafting process, but also not an insignifcant factor when compared to actively seeking out lost eggs anywhere in Creation. And individual demons might have a number of particular reasons and uses, practical or fanciful, of their own to collect such &quot;patchwork children&quot;, their particular combination of human, animal, demon, or anything else notwithstanding. That said a number of other beings in the demon kingdom might find such beings existence distasteful, offensive or unpredictable in dangerous ways for an equal number of motives and act accordingly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more of an excuse/plot hook for the occasional &quot;hell-born lost egg&quot; - or any other brand of chosen, if one wants to try out a <i>really </i>weird character background, than anything like a basis for some exalted army-building master plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}